!! Field mapping

|!OKF key |!Tiddler field |!Notes |
|`type` |`okf.type` |No field when it equals the default type; a TW content type (e.g. `text/markdown` from frontmatter) is dropped |
|`title` |`caption` |In frontmatter files (no OKF `type`, no `tw.title`) `title` is the tiddler title |
|`tw.title` |`title` |Written only when the path can't reproduce the title |
|`tags` |`tags` |Block or flow list |
|`description` |`description` | |
|`resource`, `status`, `stale_after` |`okf.resource`, `okf.status`, `okf.stale_after` |Plain text |
|`generated`, `verified`, `sources`, `usage_window` |`okf.generated`, … |JSON; filter with `jsonget` |
|`created`, `modified` |`created`, `modified` |TW dates; written as ISO 8601 UTC (`2026-01-02T03:04:05.006Z`) |
|`list` |`list` |TW list |
|other scalar keys |same name |e.g. `owner: team:finance` → field `owner` |
|other nested keys |`okf.extra` |YAML of all such keys, merged back on save |

Fields `text`, `type`, `bag`, `revision` are never written. The tiddler type of loaded OKF files is the configured tiddler type.

!! Configuration

|!Tiddler |!Default |!Meaning |
|`$:/config/rimir/okf/filter` |(empty) |Scope filter; empty = all frontmatter `.md` files |
|`$:/config/rimir/okf/default-type` |`tiddler` |OKF `type` for tiddlers without `okf.type` |
|`$:/config/rimir/okf/tiddler-type` |`text/markdown` |TW type of loaded OKF tiddlers |

!! Scope

|!Situation |!Load |!Save |
|YAML `type` is not a TW content type |OKF |— |
|`okf.type` field set |— |OKF |
|Filter empty |OKF |OKF |
|Filter matches the tiddler alone |OKF |OKF |
|Otherwise |frontmatter |frontmatter |

A TW content type is one registered in `$tw.config.contentTypeInfo` or with a parser. Save hooks only run for markdown tiddler types (`text/markdown`, `text/x-markdown`, `text/x-frontmattered-markdown`).

!! Reserved files

`index.md` and `log.md` (in any folder) are loaded as normal tiddlers but get no default `type` on save.

!! Not supported yet

* Translating OKF links (relative file paths) to tiddler links
* Generating `index.md` / `log.md`
* Preserving YAML formatting: flow style (`{ by: …, at: … }`) is written back in block style — same data, different layout

!! Restart rules

|!Change |!Restart? |
|Any `.js` module |Yes |
|Settings |No for saves; loading uses them at the next boot |

